<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06EK">Warning <span data-tag="06EK">9.2.4.2</span>.</a> In the formulation of Proposition <a data-tag="06EH" href="/tag/06EH">9.2.4.1</a>, condition $(3)$ cannot be omitted. For example, let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}= \operatorname{N}_{\bullet }( \operatorname{\mathbf{Z}})$ be the nerve of the linearly ordered set of integers $\operatorname{\mathbf{Z}}= \{  \cdots &lt; -2 &lt; -1 &lt; 0 &lt; 1 &lt; 2 &lt; \cdots \} $, let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{+}$ be the full subcategory of $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ spanned by the even integers, and let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{-}$ be the full subcategory of $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ spanned by the odd integers. Then the $\infty $-categories $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{-}$, $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$, and $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{+}$ are filtered (Example <a data-tag="05WZ" href="/tag/05WZ">9.1.1.2</a>), and the inclusion functors $F_{-}: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{-} \hookrightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ and $F_{+}: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{+} \hookrightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ are right cofinal (Corollary <a data-tag="03U2" href="/tag/03U2">7.2.3.4</a>). However, the fiber product $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{-} \times _{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}} \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{+}$ (which coincides with the homotopy fiber product $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{-} \times _{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}^{\mathrm{h}} \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{+}$) is empty. </p>
